# Scopes NODE_OPTIONS to the `api` project's `test` Nx target only.
#
# Nx loads a project-root + target-scoped dotenv file like this one
# automatically for every task that matches <project>/.env.<target> (see
# node_modules/nx/dist/src/tasks-runner/task-env-paths.js,
# getEnvPathsForTask) - it is merged into that task's forked process env
# before the task runs, and does NOT leak into any other project's task
# (webapp:test, admin:test, ...), which is exactly the isolation
# `nx run-many --target=test --all` needs (CHANTIER-MODERNISATION.md §4,
# Phase 0bis, §7 point 5): setting NODE_OPTIONS in the invoking shell leaks
# it to every forked project process and breaks jest-preset-angular for
# webapp/admin, but a per-project .env.test only reaches `api`'s own task.
#
# `--experimental-vm-modules` is required for `nx test api` to pass once
# @nestjs/* is bumped to ~12.x under Node >=24.9 (ESM interop in
# @nestjs/common's utils/load-package.util.js - see §1.4/§4 for the full
# investigation). It is a no-op under the current NestJS 11.x / Node 22
# baseline - verified harmless (see the commit introducing this file):
# `nx test api` and `nx run-many --target=test --all` both stay green,
# Node just prints one "ExperimentalWarning: VM Modules is an experimental
# feature" line per worker to stderr.
NODE_OPTIONS=--experimental-vm-modules
